      "writtenOn": "2023-12-16T00:16:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that the existing `HostConnection` instance in the end2end tests is mostly so that we can sneak in the mock Gralloc/AHB/ANW classes. Eventually, the `end2end` tests should not know anything about any Gfxstream internals (`HostConnection`/`VirtGpuDevice`/etc) and are simply a convenient area to run tests using only GL, VK, `virtio-gpu-gfxstream-renderer.h`. I think the existing mock classes can be moved into `platform` either into the existing `rutabaga` variant or a new `rutabaga_testing`/`rutabaga_android`/whatever-name. WDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "405d421687cf19d46b0c0a0199ec232ed1b4f3bb",
