      "writtenOn": "2023-12-18T16:36:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change does move Gralloc/AHB/ANW to `TestingAndroidWsi`, with the same idea of not exposing internals.  \n\nThe `END2END_TESTS` compiler directive was needed to make the end2end tests pass.  For example, `usage3` of `VkNativeAndroidBufferAndroid` now passes in the `ahb-\u003eResourceId()`.\n\nThis is because with different `HostConnection` instances, the testing layer ends up with different instances of `RutabagaLayer` (which previously provided `resource_id`).\n\nSince `libgfxstream_backend.so` is shared, `stream_renderer_assign_id` is used to query the resource_id now.\n \nOverall, I think moving internals like `HostConnection` inside gfxstream is a good idea.  Maybe if the `VirtGpuDevice` layer is good enough, maybe we make minigbm use it long-term too and add a host build there.  Not sure how to test hwcomposer too.",
      "parentUuid": "45545aeb_bd130a55",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "405d421687cf19d46b0c0a0199ec232ed1b4f3bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
